1. Theorem 1 over a wider range: |2^k - 3^s| = 1, k <= 20000 (their range: k <= 3000)
==============================================================================
solutions (k, s, D) with k >= 0: [(1, 0, 1), (1, 1, -1), (2, 1, 1), (3, 2, -1)]
  note k = 0: 2^0 - 3^0 = 0, no solution; all four solutions have s <= k.

n in [-3000000, 3000000] with T_n = n(n+1)/2 3-smooth (direct factoring):
   [(-9, 36), (-4, 6), (-3, 3), (-2, 1), (1, 1), (2, 3), (3, 6), (8, 36)]
  edge cases: T_0 = T_(-1) = 0 is not 3-smooth; T_(-n-1) = T_n, so the negative list mirrors
  the positive one (n = -2, -3, -4, -9).  36 = T_8 = T_(-9).

