==============================================================================
3. Theorem 5 (word 1^a 0): wider range and a direct search that uses no word algebra
==============================================================================
a <= 6000 with (2^(a+1) - 3^a) | (3^a - 2^a):  (a, D, x) = [(0, 1, 0), (1, 1, 1), (2, -1, -5)]
a <= 3000 with 6^a triangular: [0, 1, 2]

direct search: every cycle with EXACTLY ONE EVEN ELEMENT meeting |n| <= 200000
  3x+1: [[0], [2, 1], [-10, -5, -7]]
  3x-1: [[0], [-2, -1], [10, 5, 7]]
  5x+1: [[0], [-2, -1]]
  5x-1: [[0], [2, 1]]
  7x+1: [[0]]
  7x-1: [[0]]
  9x+1: [[0]]
  -> 3x+1: {0}, {2,1}, {-10,-5,-7};  3x-1: mirror images;  5x+1: {0}, {-2,-1};  7x+1, 9x+1: only {0}.
  The statement is sign-symmetric (3x-1 gives the negated cycles) and separates q = 3 from q >= 5
  only by the arithmetic of |2^(a+1) - q^a| = 1.

v = n + 1:  an even step sends v -> v' = (v+1)/2, so v*v' = T_v at every even step of every
orbit (not only in cycles).  Check on 10^5 random even n, both signs:
  OK.  So 'v_bot * v_top = T_(v_top)' is automatic; the content of Theorem 5 is v_top = (3/2)^a v_bot
  with v_bot = +-2^a.
  cycle [0]
     v = [1];  even steps (v, v', v*v' = T_v): [(1, 1, 1)]
  cycle [1, 2]
     v = [2, 3];  even steps (v, v', v*v' = T_v): [(3, 2, 6)]
  cycle [-5, -7, -10]
     v = [-4, -6, -9];  even steps (v, v', v*v' = T_v): [(-9, -4, 36)]
  cycle [-17, -25, -37, -55, -82, -41, -61, -91, -136, -68, -34]
     v = [-16, -24, -36, -54, -81, -40, -60, -90, -135, -67, -33];  even steps (v, v', v*v' = T_v): [(-81, -40, 3240), (-135, -67, 9045), (-67, -33, 2211), (-33, -16, 528)]
